import React, { useState, useEffect, useMemo, useRef } from 'react';

/*
 * ============================================================================
 * hub - pbed: PBED weekend clean planner (Plan - Brief - Execute - Debrief)
 * ============================================================================
 * Version 1.0 (rebuilt from scratch, replaces pbed.txt v4.0).
 *
 * What it does
 * - Plan: one lane per line. Production stop and restart come from the production schedule (craa5__aa_prd_schd).
 *   Sanitation milestones are the equipment subcategories of the assets table (craa5_aa_assets.craa5_subcategory):
 *   the number in the name is the clean order (1 - pic first); subcategories with the same number run side by side.
 *   A milestone takes the sum of its equipment minutes (craa5_hoursrequired holds minutes) divided by its people.
 *   People are limited by the crew on shift (craa5_workshift rotation; headcount from the Shift Start board for
 *   that shift, else the Employees roster; any shift can be set by hand). Maintenance is one block per line,
 *   after the foam milestone by default, sized from its SAP work orders. OPS / FSQ steps (handoff, inspect, swab,
 *   preflight, 1st pie) wrap around the milestones and are edited on Setup.
 * - Brief: goalposts per line and people by shift, copied as text.
 * - Execute: started / done per milestone (craa5__p_milestone), with Ganttly check-offs (craa5_cleancheckoff).
 * - Debrief: plan against actual, time loss (the manager hub's craa5__m_timelosslog, kind "Weekend clean"),
 *   the biggest costs of the weekend and hours paid but not used.
 * - Work orders: paste the SAP export; each order is matched to a piece of equipment (the match is remembered
 *   per functional location and asset in craa5__p_flocmap).
 * - Crew: who is on each weekend shift. Experience (hours per area, last 56 days of Shift Start history) is
 *   worked out in the background and shown only when a name is double clicked.
 *
 * Rules this page keeps
 * - Only real Dataverse rows. A read that fails is shown on the page and on the Data tab; nothing is filled in
 *   with sample data. Own tables that do not exist yet fall back to this computer (localStorage), and say so.
 * - No lookup columns: tables point at each other with plain text keys (area key, asset guid, order number).
 * - ASCII only (GEMINI.md).
 *
 * Tables: reads craa5_aa_assets, craa5__aa_prd_schd, craa5_workshift, craa5__aa_employee, craa5_shiftplan,
 * craa5_shiftboard, craa5_shiftarchive, craa5_taskassignment, craa5_cleancheckoff. Writes craa5__p_plan,
 * craa5__p_milestone, craa5__p_workorder, craa5__p_flocmap, craa5__m_timelosslog (prompts: pbed-table-prompts.md).
 * ============================================================================
 */
